  "scientific_conclusion": [
    "Neither a smooth nonlinear scalar conditional quantile nor the frozen 221-feature oriented multiscale conditional quantile reduces tail pinball loss by the preregistered ten percent in all three development domains.",
    "At q=0.999 the local model improves over the nonlinear scalar model by only 1.4 to 2.3 percent, so adding a local marginal scale or extreme-value tail continuation is not supported as the primary repair.",
    "Rolling the V31 donor conditional-quantile field by 5 Mpc/h while keeping the query backbone fixed makes Q3 and Q4 fail in every domain and raises mean delta squared by factors of 4.34 to 18.95.",
    "The remaining failure is therefore attributed to joint donor-query spatial coupling rather than marginal conditional tail prediction. The next generator must produce a query-aligned conditional stochastic field instead of transporting a donor field independently of query structure."
  ],
